{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0246-robust-draws-in-balanced-knockout-tournaments.md", "equation": "Deterministic: wp(1,P′,σ) = 1 − c·ε + ε²Q(ε) (Lemma 5); d̂_ε = c·ε (Cor. 2).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9123}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0246-robust-draws-in-balanced-knockout-tournaments.md", "equation": "Probabilistic: wp(1,P,σ) = α_ij·P_ij + β_ij; d̂_ε = Σ_{i≠j} | (Lemma 7); Taylor: wp(1,P′,σ) = wp(1,P,σ) − εΣe_ij α_ij + ε²Q(ε), maximized by sign-matching e_ij to α_ij.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9123}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0246-robust-draws-in-balanced-knockout-tournaments.md", "equation": "Hard-tournament recursion: p_{k+1} = p_k·[p_k(1−ε) + (1−p_k)ε], p_1 = 1−ε → degree 2^n−1 polynomial, linear coefficient N−1 (Prop. 1).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9123}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0246-robust-draws-in-balanced-knockout-tournaments.md", "equation": "Example 1: 2-round tournament, σ=(1,2,3,4): wp(1) = 0.9³ = 0.729, wp(2)=0, wp(3)=0.171, wp(4)=0.1; draws (1,3,2,4),(1,4,2,3) give wp(1)=0.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9123}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0246-robust-draws-in-balanced-knockout-tournaments.md", "equation": "Example 2** (6-round hard tournament, N=64, unique winning draw): wp(1,P′,σ) = 1 − 63ε + … − 2147483648ε^63; wp_0.01 < 0.54, wp_0.05 < 0.07, wp_0.1 < 0.02 — a \"guaranteed\" win collapses under 1% probability error.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9123}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0246-robust-draws-in-balanced-knockout-tournaments.md", "equation": "Example 3** (unbalanced 6-round): both draws give wp=1 exactly, but wp_0.01: <0.73 vs >0.89; wp_0.05: <0.23 vs >0.56; wp_0.1: <0.08 vs >0.31. Robust draw: wp_ε ≥ (1−ε)^11.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9123}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0246-robust-draws-in-balanced-knockout-tournaments.md", "equation": "Example 4** (6-round, small/medium/big): mwp(1,P) = wp(1,P,σ) > 0.506 (optimal); suboptimal σ′: wp = 0.502; but wp_0.02: <0.429 (optimal) vs >0.432 (suboptimal) — the suboptimal draw guarantees more.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9123}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0246-robust-draws-in-balanced-knockout-tournaments.md", "equation": "Linear-term approximation only:** d̂_ε ignores ε²+ terms; Example 2's polynomial shows higher-order terms dominate quickly (−2.1×10^9·ε^63) — the \"sufficiently small ε\" regime (ε < cN^{−2}) is extremely restrictive for N=64 (ε ≪ 0.0002).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9123}
